//! Pi Engine - Atomic operation engine for Aleph
//!
//! This module implements the Pi engine, inspired by OpenClaw's architecture,
//! providing atomic operations (Read, Write, Edit, Bash) with:
//!
//! - Token efficiency: 80-95% reduction through incremental editing
//! - Fast routing: L1/L2 reflex layer for millisecond responses
//! - Self-healing: Automatic error recovery and retry logic
//!
//! # Architecture
//!
//! ```text
//! ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//! │                        PiEngine                              │
//! ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
//! │  L1: Exact Match Cache    → < 10ms                          │
//! │  L2: Keyword Routing      → < 50ms                          │
//! │  L3: LLM Reasoning        → 1-3s                            │
//! └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//! ```
//!
//! # Example
//!
//! ```rust,ignore
//! use alephcore::pi::{AtomicAction, Patch, PatchApplier};
//!
//! // Create a patch to modify a file
//! let patch = Patch {
//!     start_line: 10,
//!     end_line: 12,
//!     old_content: "old code".to_string(),
//!     new_content: "new code".to_string(),
//! };
//!
//! // Apply the patch
//! let action = AtomicAction::Edit {
//!     path: "src/main.rs".to_string(),
//!     patches: vec![patch],
//! };
//! ```

